first time in more than half a century  congress will hold a public hearing on  one of history's great mysteries ufos  for the first time in over 50 years a  subcommittee in the house of  representatives is holding an open  congressional hearing on uaps  the term unidentified aerial phenomena  has replaced the unidentified flying  object or ufo the public now has a  chance to hear directly from experts and  leaders in the intelligence community on  one of history's greatest mysteries  pentagon officials have been  tight-lipped on the details but here's  what we do know there have been nearly  150 reports of unidentified aerial  phenomena since 2004. only one of which  was explained in a report that led the  pentagon to form a special program meant  to streamline data surrounding the  unexplained occurrences intelligence  committee chairman adam schiff says he  hopes to break the cycle of excessive  secrecy and speculation with truth and  transparency the hearing will be  followed by a closed classified hearing  on that pentagon program that was  recently established
 

